{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/math\/customdimensions"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Extending-the-Framework","title":"Extending the Framework","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CustomDimensions"},"abstract":[{"text":"Extend ","type":"text"},{"code":"Math","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with your own physical dimensions and units—currency, points, gameplay metrics, or anything else your app measures.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Math"}],"title":"Custom Dimensions and Units","role":"article"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Math"},{"text":" ships with a comprehensive set of base dimensions (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/length"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/time"},{"text":", and friends) and derived dimensions (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/speed"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/energy","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and more). These cover physics and everyday measurement, but your app almost certainly measures things that aren’t in the SI system too: money, hit points, ingredients, resource points, users, and so on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The good news: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is an open system. Because a dimension is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"just a dictionary of exponent powers","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", you can describe any dimension you can imagine at runtime.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Define a Custom Dimension","type":"heading","anchor":"Define-a-Custom-Dimension"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with a dictionary of exponent identifiers. Each key is a dimension name and each value is its power:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Math","","\/\/ A dimension for money, with a single base exponent.","let usdDimension = PhysicalDimension(exponents: [\"USD\": 1])","","\/\/ A dimension for \"users\", used later in per-user metrics.","let userDimension = PhysicalDimension(exponents: [\"user\": 1])"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can build compound custom dimensions with the same arithmetic used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internally: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+"},{"text":" multiplies dimensions, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":" divides them, and "},{"code":"*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" raises a dimension to a power:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let revenuePerUser = usdDimension - userDimension   \/\/ [\"USD\": 1, \"user\": -1]"]},{"level":3,"text":"Define Custom Units","type":"heading","anchor":"Define-Custom-Units"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom dimensions don’t have a compile-time type, so use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/unknown","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as the type-level parameter and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/NamedUnit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"create units. Pass a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/LinearConverter","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" (for a simple scale) or an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/OffsetConverter","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (for a scale plus an offset) to handle conversions:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let usdUnit = NamedUnit<MathDimension.unknown>(","    symbol: \"$\",","    dimension: usdDimension,","    converter: LinearConverter(coefficient: 1.0)",")","","\/\/ EUR is defined relative to the same base dimension.","let eurUnit = NamedUnit<MathDimension.unknown>(","    symbol: \"€\",","    dimension: usdDimension,","    converter: LinearConverter(coefficient: 1.09)",")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keep the same ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PhysicalDimension"},{"text":" value (here ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"usdDimension"},{"text":") for every","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unit in a family. The framework only converts between units whose dimensions"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"match, so sharing the exact same value makes your money interchangeable."}]}],"style":"tip","name":"Tip","type":"aside"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Convert-Between-Custom-Units","text":"Convert Between Custom Units","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Custom units convert exactly like the built-in ones:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let walletInEur = Quantity(value: 100.0, unit: eurUnit)","let walletInUsd = walletInEur.converted(to: usdUnit)","","print(walletInUsd.value) \/\/ 109.0"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Combine Custom Units with Built-In Ones","anchor":"Combine-Custom-Units-with-Built-In-Ones","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom dimensions participate in dimensional arithmetic too. Here a currency"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension combines with the built-in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/time","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" dimension:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let hourlyRate = Quantity(value: 50.0, unit: usdUnit) \/ Quantity(value: 1.0, unit: Units.hour)","","print(hourlyRate.value)          \/\/ 50.0","print(hourlyRate.unit.dimension) \/\/ [\"USD\": 1, \"time\": -1]","print(hourlyRate.unit.symbol)    \/\/ \"($\/h)\""]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Use-the-Currency-Dimension","text":"Use the Currency Dimension"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If your custom dimension happens to be currency, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Math"},{"type":"text","text":" already defines a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/currency","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" dimension and a built-in library of world"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"currencies (and cryptocurrencies) in ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units"},{"type":"text","text":". Currency units automatically"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"place their symbol before the value when formatting:"}]},{"code":["let gift = Quantity(value: 100.0, unit: Units.usd)","print(gift.formatted()) \/\/ \"$100.00\"","","\/\/ Resolve units from ISO 4217 codes at runtime.","if let currency = Units.currency(for: \"SEK\") {","    print(currency.symbol) \/\/ \"kr\"","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Whats-Next","text":"What’s Next?"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to lock custom units into a compile-time dimension in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Explore ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units"},{"text":" to see the breadth of units provided out of the box.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"references":{"doc://Math/documentation/Math/LinearConverter":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/LinearConverter","title":"LinearConverter","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinearConverter"}],"url":"\/documentation\/math\/linearconverter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/UnitConverter"},{"type":"text","text":" that scales values by a fixed coefficient."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinearConverter"}]},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/PhysicalDimension/energy":{"title":"energy","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The dimension of energy ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"force × length"},{"type":"text","text":", SI unit: joule)."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/math\/physicaldimension\/energy","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"energy","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": `Self`","kind":"te